1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
= kissasia.co =

2
00:00:00,166 --> 00:00:01,142
[This is a fictional story. All characters and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,166 --> 00:00:02,143
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:03,709
[under the guardian and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:06,933
[Episode 9]

6
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:22,467
You startled me!

7
00:00:24,622 --> 00:00:27,666
- What are you doing?
- Huh? What is it?

8
00:00:28,382 --> 00:00:33,233
I feel like I said something important and heard something even more important.

9
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,499
Wow, I never knew there was honey tea in the break room.

10
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:43,026
You don't usually drink like that.

11
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,431
You should've gone home and become one with your bed.

12
00:00:45,455 --> 00:00:47,045
Why'd you come in on the weekend?

13
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:50,230
Why did you come in, then?

14
00:00:50,254 --> 00:00:55,233
Me? Are you asking me? Are you genuinely curious?

15
00:00:56,057 --> 00:01:00,499
Then shall I give you a sincere answer?

16
00:01:01,202 --> 00:01:03,209
"Look into the unusual death in Hyeonsa-dong."

17
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:06,409
"Pull a list of the punks recently released who didn't serve enough time."

18
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:08,118
You're making my head spin.

19
00:01:08,142 --> 00:01:11,830
My head's already not exactly in working order.

20
00:01:11,854 --> 00:01:14,962
[Violent Crimes Team 2] And that's not all. See this?

21
00:01:14,986 --> 00:01:17,442
Endless Kingfisher material?

22
00:01:17,466 --> 00:01:18,664
This is why I'm...

23
00:01:18,688 --> 00:01:21,166
Need to take the exam again?

24
00:01:24,754 --> 00:01:27,764
[Kingfisher Case Files] Let's see. Today...

25
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:29,110
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon Case] Oh, Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

26
00:01:29,134 --> 00:01:30,346
Oh, this is that case.

27
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:32,958
Kingfisher's last case before disappearing.

28
00:01:34,066 --> 00:01:36,433
I think I'm finally getting somewhere.

29
00:01:39,659 --> 00:01:41,578
[Haegong-dong Case Overview]

30
00:01:42,588 --> 00:01:44,757
[With seven-year-old Yeon Cheol present] Huh? What's this?

31
00:01:44,781 --> 00:01:47,593
There was a seven-year-old child at the scene?

32
00:01:47,617 --> 00:01:51,422
But there's a side of him people don't know.

33
00:01:51,446 --> 00:01:54,622
A punk who shot a dad dead

34
00:01:54,646 --> 00:01:58,238
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

35
00:01:58,262 --> 00:01:59,934
Actually, I know.

36
00:01:59,958 --> 00:02:03,366
I'm telling you, I saw Kingfisher.

37
00:02:04,433 --> 00:02:09,894
I was there at the Haegong-dong Gosiwon case that day.

38
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:12,233
- Ah!
- Oh, you startled me!

39
00:02:14,632 --> 00:02:18,098
Bo Na, you didn't answer, so I left a message.

40
00:02:18,122 --> 00:02:19,912
Did you just see it?

41
00:02:19,936 --> 00:02:21,408
You pulled another prank on me?

42
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:23,209
Oh, jeez.

43
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:26,798
I figured you'd be home since it's the weekend.

44
00:02:26,822 --> 00:02:29,226
Was I being rude?

45
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,454
Should I wait out here?

46
00:02:31,478 --> 00:02:34,699
You can wait inside if you don't mind.

47
00:02:36,399 --> 00:02:37,409
[Bo Na]

48
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:38,490
[Speakerphone]

49
00:02:38,514 --> 00:02:41,433
Bo Na, is it okay if I do that?

50
00:02:43,166 --> 00:02:45,418
Listen carefully.

51
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:47,631
If you say even one useless word,

52
00:02:47,655 --> 00:02:50,546
you'll die by my hand.

53
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:53,446
That's hurtful. You don't trust me?

54
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:58,252
Back then and now, ever since "that day."

55
00:02:58,276 --> 00:03:02,274
If you don't want to die, you'd better remember what I said.

56
00:03:02,298 --> 00:03:04,866
Thanks for welcoming me, Bo Na.

57
00:03:05,626 --> 00:03:08,433
Come quickly. I miss you.

58
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:13,210
Please come on in.

59
00:03:21,288 --> 00:03:24,342
Congratulations. You're pregnant.

60
00:03:24,366 --> 00:03:26,282
You're five weeks along.

61
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:27,283
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"]

62
00:03:27,307 --> 00:03:30,170
Right here, do you see this little bean?

63
00:03:30,194 --> 00:03:31,582
That's the gestational sac.

64
00:03:31,606 --> 00:03:33,046
The gestational sac?

65
00:03:33,070 --> 00:03:35,275
Yeah.

66
00:03:35,299 --> 00:03:36,934
[Prenatal Care Booklet]

67
00:03:36,958 --> 00:03:39,762
You're still in the early stages, so you need to be extra careful, okay?

68
00:03:39,786 --> 00:03:43,702
Avoid running, strenuous exercise, and lifting heavy objects.

69
00:03:43,726 --> 00:03:45,454
It's also best to avoid rushing up and down stairs

70
00:03:45,478 --> 00:03:50,186
or making sudden movements like sitting down and standing up quickly.

71
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:53,986
Most importantly, try to stay relaxed.

72
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:57,266
Stress can have a negative effect.

73
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:03,209
[Calls]

74
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:05,299
[My Santa]

75
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:10,709
[Incoming Call, My Santa]

76
00:04:10,733 --> 00:04:12,833
[My Santa]

77
00:04:14,238 --> 00:04:15,215
Tae Seong.

78
00:04:15,239 --> 00:04:17,302
Yeah, honey. Did you have lunch?

79
00:04:17,326 --> 00:04:19,122
Of course. Look at the time. I ate ages ago.

80
00:04:19,146 --> 00:04:20,182
What about you, Tae Seong?

81
00:04:20,206 --> 00:04:21,978
I'm on my way to get something to eat.

82
00:04:22,002 --> 00:04:24,570
I just finished an interview.

83
00:04:24,594 --> 00:04:26,118
You must be starving.

84
00:04:26,142 --> 00:04:28,099
What's wrong with your voice?

85
00:04:28,845 --> 00:04:30,545
Are you sick?

86
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:35,099
No, I'm perfectly fine. Why do you ask?

87
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,954
Are you going to be late today?

88
00:04:38,978 --> 00:04:42,586
Even if I leave right after lunch,

89
00:04:42,610 --> 00:04:44,126
I'll probably have to stop by the office,

90
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:46,574
so it'll be evening by the time I get there.

91
00:04:46,598 --> 00:04:48,366
I wish you could come early.

92
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:50,098
[Prenatal Care Booklet] So we can have dinner together.

93
00:04:50,122 --> 00:04:52,474
I have something to show you.

94
00:04:52,498 --> 00:04:56,666
Of course, I'll come early. I'll wrap things up and fly home.

95
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:09,973
Have you figured out what you're going to do next?

96
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:10,974
Not really.

97
00:05:10,998 --> 00:05:14,654
I was thinking of opening a little shop with my severance pay,

98
00:05:14,678 --> 00:05:16,602
but I don't have anything specific in mind.

99
00:05:16,626 --> 00:05:18,558
If I had my way,

100
00:05:18,582 --> 00:05:22,690
I'd like to spend the rest of my life looking at beautiful things.

101
00:05:22,714 --> 00:05:25,933
Then you should open a flower shop. Flowers are beautiful.

102
00:05:27,642 --> 00:05:30,282
Hey, wow!

103
00:05:30,306 --> 00:05:35,014
Even Yoo Bo Na knows flowers are pretty. Feels like a whole different era.

104
00:05:35,038 --> 00:05:38,406
Well, I guess the world has changed.

105
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,566
Your world has.

106
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,442
Well, you look so much brighter too.

107
00:05:43,466 --> 00:05:45,699
I guess married life is treating you well, huh?

108
00:05:55,402 --> 00:06:00,399
But once the baby arrives, does the world really change?

109
00:06:05,534 --> 00:06:07,466
Are you planning to have a baby?

110
00:06:10,274 --> 00:06:12,382
I can't quite explain how I feel.

111
00:06:12,406 --> 00:06:14,306
It scares me too.

112
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:19,470
The word "mom" just feels so far away from me.

113
00:06:19,494 --> 00:06:21,234
You're worrying about nothing.

114
00:06:21,258 --> 00:06:23,106
You'll still be you after you become a mom.

115
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:26,314
"Your world won't change. It just gets bigger."

116
00:06:26,338 --> 00:06:29,233
That's what my grandma always used to say.

117
00:06:30,058 --> 00:06:32,366
And that's what I believed too.

118
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:36,790
Do you think I can really do this?

119
00:06:36,814 --> 00:06:38,866
You're already doing a great job.

120
00:06:39,934 --> 00:06:44,899
You've got herbal tea in front of you instead of your beloved coffee.

121
00:06:48,522 --> 00:06:50,102
Don't worry.

122
00:06:50,126 --> 00:06:52,822
Your world has already changed once.

123
00:06:52,846 --> 00:06:57,666
It's only going to get bigger and stronger from now on.

124
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:14,918
- Yes, Team Leader.
- Oh, Director Yoo.

125
00:07:14,942 --> 00:07:18,130
The Yeon Chang Bok meeting today has fallen through.

126
00:07:18,154 --> 00:07:19,809
Ugh, that darn punk...

127
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:23,442
He made a move before Manager Go could do anything.

128
00:07:23,466 --> 00:07:24,718
Yeah.

129
00:07:24,742 --> 00:07:28,042
I'm chasing him right now. He's getting away in a taxi.

130
00:07:28,066 --> 00:07:29,562
He moved faster than we expected.

131
00:07:29,586 --> 00:07:34,622
Who knew he'd change his mind the second he got to the hospital?

132
00:07:34,646 --> 00:07:36,875
If we lose him now,

133
00:07:36,899 --> 00:07:40,798
I don't think we'll get another chance to catch him easily.

134
00:07:40,822 --> 00:07:44,075
We need to revise the scenario. I'll go.

135
00:07:44,099 --> 00:07:46,299
Keep me updated on his route.

136
00:08:54,766 --> 00:08:56,075
What did you bring?

137
00:08:56,099 --> 00:08:57,507
Forget that. The money!

138
00:08:57,531 --> 00:08:59,231
Here.

139
00:09:10,658 --> 00:09:11,842
- Team Leader.
- Yeah?

140
00:09:11,866 --> 00:09:14,102
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon] Yeon Chang Bok's mom and son are here.

141
00:09:14,126 --> 00:09:15,242
A son?

142
00:09:15,266 --> 00:09:18,258
The newborn his mom was holding when he was arrested.

143
00:09:18,282 --> 00:09:21,082
Yeah, I'll wait until they leave.

144
00:09:21,106 --> 00:09:23,062
The police are about to storm in.

145
00:09:23,086 --> 00:09:24,314
This doesn't look good.

146
00:09:24,338 --> 00:09:26,270
Not in front of the kid.

147
00:09:26,294 --> 00:09:27,994
I'll just wait.

148
00:09:30,479 --> 00:09:31,974
Surprise!

149
00:09:31,998 --> 00:09:34,299
Hi, my friend.

150
00:09:50,582 --> 00:09:52,122
- It came out again.
- Right?

151
00:09:52,146 --> 00:09:53,646
Isn't it awesome?

152
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,902
- Another one!
- There it is again.

153
00:09:55,926 --> 00:09:57,838
Honey, you're back?

154
00:09:57,862 --> 00:09:58,839
Mommy!

155
00:09:58,863 --> 00:10:01,438
More and more toys keep coming out of the doll.

156
00:10:01,462 --> 00:10:02,638
Yeah?

157
00:10:02,662 --> 00:10:06,166
Sergei brought another gift for Yul.

158
00:10:07,122 --> 00:10:08,666
You should've told me you were coming.

159
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,566
Surprise!

160
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:13,866
Hi, my friend.

161
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,738
It's here, it's here!

162
00:10:16,762 --> 00:10:19,275
- What's here?
- Chicken! Chicken's here!

163
00:10:19,299 --> 00:10:23,350
I think your husband's jealous of us.

164
00:10:23,374 --> 00:10:26,333
Behave yourself.

165
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:29,518
[Tae Seong Chicken] I didn't have anything proper to serve him,

166
00:10:29,542 --> 00:10:32,006
so I asked Sun II for a favor.

167
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:34,622
I could've just taken him out for dinner.

168
00:10:34,646 --> 00:10:37,209
You're not feeling well. Why go through all that trouble?

169
00:10:37,233 --> 00:10:41,833
No, I'm fine. I told you I wanted to see your Russian friend too.

170
00:10:43,902 --> 00:10:46,310
I didn't know he was that kind of man.

171
00:10:46,334 --> 00:10:48,238
Didn't I tell you he was a man?

172
00:10:48,262 --> 00:10:49,894
I think I did.

173
00:10:49,918 --> 00:10:52,166
Yeah, you said he was a man.

174
00:10:52,899 --> 00:10:56,146
You just didn't say he was that good-looking.

175
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:58,278
- Huh?
- What?

176
00:10:58,302 --> 00:10:59,862
You think he's a good-looking man?

177
00:10:59,886 --> 00:11:01,122
He's pretty handsome.

178
00:11:01,146 --> 00:11:03,066
You, seriously...

179
00:11:04,534 --> 00:11:06,589
Let's go eat too.

180
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:14,262
Korean fried chicken really is the best.

181
00:11:14,286 --> 00:11:15,618
It's so good.

182
00:11:15,642 --> 00:11:18,242
I'm glad it suits your taste.

183
00:11:18,266 --> 00:11:20,710
But Sergei...

184
00:11:20,734 --> 00:11:24,158
Just call me Seul Gi. That's easier.

185
00:11:24,182 --> 00:11:25,286
I'm good with that too.

186
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,266
Oh, alright.

187
00:11:28,834 --> 00:11:33,154
Seul Gi, I heard you were born in Russia.

188
00:11:33,178 --> 00:11:34,802
But your Korean is really good.

189
00:11:34,826 --> 00:11:38,386
My mama is Korean.

190
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:42,499
And I got used to the language from playing with Bo Na since we were kids.

191
00:11:45,998 --> 00:11:48,810
Yeah, we lived in the same neighborhood back then.

192
00:11:48,834 --> 00:11:52,638
I think I first met Bo Na when we were eight.

193
00:11:52,662 --> 00:11:55,634
Right after you moved to Russia, remember?

194
00:11:55,658 --> 00:11:57,326
You're right.

195
00:11:57,350 --> 00:12:00,133
So you've known each other for a long time.

196
00:12:00,890 --> 00:12:03,130
We have.

197
00:12:03,154 --> 00:12:05,658
By the way, are you okay, honey?

198
00:12:05,682 --> 00:12:09,109
Well, he came home so wasted last night that he blacked out.

199
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,142
- You must be exhausted.
- No...

200
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:12,362
- Can you really eat this right now?
- No, I'm fine. I'm really fine.

201
00:12:12,386 --> 00:12:16,038
I just enjoy hearing about your past.

202
00:12:16,062 --> 00:12:17,318
- It's good.
- I'm fine.

203
00:12:17,342 --> 00:12:18,738
Well, it's...

204
00:12:18,762 --> 00:12:20,462
When I first met Bo Na,

205
00:12:20,486 --> 00:12:26,130
I said in Korean, "Hi, I'm Sergei."

206
00:12:26,154 --> 00:12:27,786
And she goes, "Seul Gi?"

207
00:12:27,810 --> 00:12:30,270
"No, Sergei."

208
00:12:30,294 --> 00:12:33,666
"Ah! No Seul Gi?"

209
00:12:38,990 --> 00:12:44,218
From that day on, I was just "No Seul Gi" to Bo Na.

210
00:12:44,242 --> 00:12:46,475
So that's the story behind your nickname.

211
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:50,006
Yul, chew this slowly and thoroughly, okay?

212
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:51,666
Mommy, you eat some too.

213
00:12:51,690 --> 00:12:53,499
Is this for me?

214
00:12:54,466 --> 00:12:55,926
It's good. Thank you.

215
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:58,030
Bo Na, are you eating chicken?

216
00:12:58,054 --> 00:12:59,870
You never used to like chicken.

217
00:12:59,894 --> 00:13:00,990
I do now.

218
00:13:01,014 --> 00:13:03,634
Really? That's interesting.

219
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:06,114
You used to hate the smell of chicken...

220
00:13:06,138 --> 00:13:08,262
Oh, chicken porridge!

221
00:13:08,286 --> 00:13:10,499
You didn't like chicken porridge either.

222
00:13:11,866 --> 00:13:13,786
- Huh?
- Back then, I did.

223
00:13:13,810 --> 00:13:18,433
It seems there are still a lot of things you don't know about Bo Na.

224
00:13:19,722 --> 00:13:22,199
Or does she just not tell you much about herself?

225
00:13:25,222 --> 00:13:29,575
When Bo Na was in school, some mean kids used to play pranks on her.

226
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:33,582
They'd secretly dunk her chicken in muddy water,

227
00:13:33,606 --> 00:13:37,506
or pour strong whiskey into her chicken soup.

228
00:13:37,530 --> 00:13:39,799
So sometimes

229
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:43,133
things got physical.

230
00:13:44,606 --> 00:13:47,546
Bo Na was pretty tough back then.

231
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:49,709
Hey, you don't need to bring that up.

232
00:13:49,733 --> 00:13:55,254
In Korean, we'd say "no mercy."

233
00:13:55,278 --> 00:13:58,570
Bo Na is very self-assured and clear about what she wants in everything.

234
00:13:58,594 --> 00:14:00,799
She knows exactly what's right and wrong.

235
00:14:01,906 --> 00:14:03,362
- Is that so?
- Yeah.

236
00:14:03,386 --> 00:14:06,594
And Bo Na eats chicken just fine now. She even likes chicken porridge.

237
00:14:06,618 --> 00:14:09,375
Food tastes different depending on

238
00:14:09,399 --> 00:14:14,290
who you eat it with and what memories it holds, right?

239
00:14:14,314 --> 00:14:16,414
Oh, I see.

240
00:14:16,438 --> 00:14:18,766
I may not have known the Bo Na from childhood,

241
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:20,986
but I know who she is now.

242
00:14:21,010 --> 00:14:25,170
Because what matters is the present, not the past.

243
00:14:25,194 --> 00:14:26,894
Isn't it?

244
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:32,118
I was curious what kind of man Bo Na would end up with.

245
00:14:32,142 --> 00:14:33,930
Looks like she found a good one.

246
00:14:33,954 --> 00:14:37,666
Oh, no. I'm the one who got lucky enough to meet an amazing woman.

247
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:43,009
He is so tired now.

248
00:14:43,033 --> 00:14:46,810
Let's finish up and go have some tea, okay?

249
00:14:46,834 --> 00:14:48,534
Alright.

250
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:57,490
We'll just have tea and come right back.

251
00:14:57,514 --> 00:14:59,514
I'll be back soon, Yul, okay?

252
00:14:59,538 --> 00:15:00,515
Take your time.

253
00:15:00,539 --> 00:15:03,599
You two must have a lot to catch up on after all this time.

254
00:15:04,746 --> 00:15:07,130
Thanks for the great chicken and the wonderful conversation.

255
00:15:07,154 --> 00:15:09,609
- Let's catch up again soon.
- Okay.

256
00:15:12,734 --> 00:15:14,730
Goodbye! Little Yul.

257
00:15:14,754 --> 00:15:16,933
Goodbye.

258
00:15:20,478 --> 00:15:23,033
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

259
00:16:04,829 --> 00:16:07,806
Oh, Bo Na, calm down.

260
00:16:07,830 --> 00:16:10,533
I told you not to show your face in front of me again, didn't I?

261
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:15,399
Just as I thought, those two are your Achilles' heels.

262
00:16:16,562 --> 00:16:20,430
Looks like my warning that day wasn't strong enough.

263
00:16:20,454 --> 00:16:25,966
Having something to protect is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

264
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:34,346
Okay.

265
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:37,226
I'm not coming back.

266
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,142
I promise you.

267
00:16:39,166 --> 00:16:41,766
That's your second warning.

268
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,599
No third chance.

269
00:16:45,314 --> 00:16:47,014
Get lost.

270
00:16:47,982 --> 00:16:50,133
I really meant it.

271
00:16:54,058 --> 00:16:56,999
You seem to have found a good guy.

272
00:17:35,233 --> 00:17:36,575
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"] No way!

273
00:17:36,599 --> 00:17:39,738
It seems like Yeon Chang Bok escaped from the hospital while in medical custody.

274
00:17:39,762 --> 00:17:41,818
Yeon Chang Bok?

275
00:17:41,842 --> 00:17:43,733
Yeon Chang Bok...

276
00:17:45,150 --> 00:17:46,640
Oh, that guy...

277
00:17:46,664 --> 00:17:50,202
The aggravated sex offender who broke into a home and threatened the family?

278
00:17:50,226 --> 00:17:52,025
The lowest of the low.

279
00:17:52,049 --> 00:17:55,074
He pointed the knife at the victim's baby, not even the victim herself.

280
00:17:55,098 --> 00:17:57,502
The mom eventually took her own life a few months later.

281
00:17:57,526 --> 00:17:59,958
Right, you covered that case too, didn't you?

282
00:17:59,982 --> 00:18:01,306
Yeah, for a day.

283
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:06,402
The day Yeon Chang Bok's mom protested outside the courthouse for leniency.

284
00:18:06,426 --> 00:18:09,454
Yeah, I accompanied the mom and followed her to her house.

285
00:18:09,478 --> 00:18:11,402
And I even saw Yeon Chang Bok's son.

286
00:18:11,426 --> 00:18:15,099
Someone like that should be taken out by Kingfisher.

287
00:18:15,810 --> 00:18:17,609
So, are you a Kingfisher fan too, Mr. Nam?

288
00:18:17,633 --> 00:18:21,194
Oh, a lot of reporters secretly support him, actually.

289
00:18:21,218 --> 00:18:22,734
Hold on.

290
00:18:22,758 --> 00:18:25,575
At this rate, won't Kingfisher find this punk first?

291
00:18:25,599 --> 00:18:29,009
He's always a step ahead of the cops.

292
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:32,662
Honestly, that might be better than getting caught by the police.

293
00:18:32,686 --> 00:18:35,602
Sorry, Mr. Nam, but I think I should go into the office alone.

294
00:18:35,626 --> 00:18:38,066
What? Why?

295
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:44,866
Hey, reckless young man.

296
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:51,690
You need to learn that some doors in this world should never be opened.

297
00:20:53,662 --> 00:20:55,214
Surprise!

298
00:20:55,238 --> 00:20:57,466
Hi, my friend.

299
00:21:01,034 --> 00:21:02,833
I'll be offline for a bit.

300
00:21:03,602 --> 00:21:04,910
What are you doing here?

301
00:21:04,934 --> 00:21:07,534
Why are you...

302
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:09,833
How did you know I was here?

303
00:21:17,626 --> 00:21:20,166
Still got those sticky fingers, I see.

304
00:21:21,318 --> 00:21:22,490
What's going on today?

305
00:21:22,514 --> 00:21:25,894
Why are you letting your guard down? That's not like you.

306
00:21:25,918 --> 00:21:26,898
What brings you to Korea?

307
00:21:26,922 --> 00:21:29,109
I was bored, so I came to visit.

308
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:31,842
Russia is too boring without you.

309
00:21:31,866 --> 00:21:33,999
Go. I'm working now.

310
00:21:35,694 --> 00:21:38,238
Well, is there a problem?

311
00:21:38,262 --> 00:21:41,466
The client has a visitor, so I'm standing by.

312
00:21:46,282 --> 00:21:48,542
Now that's more like you.

313
00:21:48,566 --> 00:21:52,194
But once the guest leaves, you can do it?

314
00:21:52,218 --> 00:21:53,685
You're still in the very early stages,

315
00:21:53,709 --> 00:21:56,633
so I think you were told to be extra careful.

316
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:01,133
Where did you even...

317
00:22:01,818 --> 00:22:03,538
Isn't this the time

318
00:22:03,562 --> 00:22:06,766
when you should be focusing on nothing but beautiful things?

319
00:22:08,182 --> 00:22:13,466
But if you absolutely have to do it, how about hiring a mercenary?

320
00:22:19,638 --> 00:22:21,454
A mercenary?

321
00:22:21,478 --> 00:22:23,699
The best mercenary.

322
00:22:31,774 --> 00:22:35,166
Then you just pull the trigger. I'll take care of the rest.

323
00:22:35,970 --> 00:22:37,906
Wise choice.

324
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:40,714
Not yet, wait.

325
00:22:40,738 --> 00:22:43,499
I need to confirm the location first.

326
00:22:55,430 --> 00:22:58,299
Is there just one guest?

327
00:23:00,390 --> 00:23:02,090
Oh.

328
00:23:02,726 --> 00:23:04,402
A young boy?

329
00:23:04,426 --> 00:23:05,578
His son.

330
00:23:05,602 --> 00:23:09,175
Once the child has left, then...

331
00:23:09,199 --> 00:23:10,309
Target is down.

332
00:23:10,333 --> 00:23:12,399
What on earth are you doing?

333
00:23:19,366 --> 00:23:22,442
Calm down, Bo Na.

334
00:23:22,466 --> 00:23:25,738
You crazy punk! You want to die?

335
00:23:25,762 --> 00:23:30,609
The person holding the gun decides when to pull the trigger.

336
00:23:30,633 --> 00:23:33,790
- You know that.
- The boy is innocent.

337
00:23:33,814 --> 00:23:35,318
He's done nothing wrong.

338
00:23:35,342 --> 00:23:41,166
"Your name, in death, only ends up on your tombstone."

339
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:47,426
"But your sins, even in death, are passed down to your children."

340
00:23:47,450 --> 00:23:49,442
That's what Mama always used to say.

341
00:23:49,466 --> 00:23:51,199
Shut up!

342
00:23:59,618 --> 00:24:02,182
Did I kill a kid like someone else did?

343
00:24:02,206 --> 00:24:04,254
I didn't, right?

344
00:24:04,278 --> 00:24:05,786
So isn't that enough?

345
00:24:05,810 --> 00:24:08,982
Oh, calm down, Bo Na.

346
00:24:09,006 --> 00:24:11,999
The doctor said stress isn't good for the baby...

347
00:24:44,599 --> 00:24:45,875
[Not Today, Kwon Tae Seong]

348
00:24:45,899 --> 00:24:48,333
Kwon Tae Seong?

349
00:24:49,462 --> 00:24:51,162
So he's a reporter?

350
00:24:52,734 --> 00:24:54,434
And what's this?

351
00:24:58,810 --> 00:25:00,766
Interesting.

352
00:25:28,554 --> 00:25:30,254
You're awake.

353
00:25:32,006 --> 00:25:34,354
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong.

354
00:25:34,378 --> 00:25:39,199
Forget everything that happened today.

355
00:25:39,942 --> 00:25:44,699
And from now on, you'd better stop looking into Kingfisher.

356
00:25:46,930 --> 00:25:49,333
If you break your promise,

357
00:25:50,586 --> 00:25:54,102
your wife and your child,

358
00:25:54,126 --> 00:25:56,866
your family could be in danger.

359
00:26:02,754 --> 00:26:04,242
Calm down.

360
00:26:04,266 --> 00:26:07,274
Shh.

361
00:26:07,298 --> 00:26:11,833
As long as you keep your promise, nothing will happen.

362
00:26:13,286 --> 00:26:15,566
Well, then...

363
00:26:21,198 --> 00:26:23,766
Goodnight, Tae Seong.

364
00:26:29,782 --> 00:26:33,462
Why are you still so angry, Yoo Bo Na?

365
00:26:33,486 --> 00:26:38,422
Did I put a blemish on Kingfisher's flawless record?

366
00:26:38,446 --> 00:26:43,154
You left a scar on a child that he'll never forget for the rest of his life.

367
00:26:43,178 --> 00:26:46,394
Did I force you to give up the gun?

368
00:26:46,418 --> 00:26:48,322
You were the one who chose.

369
00:26:48,346 --> 00:26:53,162
Don't you have to give something up to protect something else?

370
00:26:53,186 --> 00:26:55,322
You're wrong.

371
00:26:55,346 --> 00:26:57,934
It wasn't a sacrifice. It was a mistake.

372
00:26:57,958 --> 00:27:00,058
My mistake was trusting you for a moment

373
00:27:00,082 --> 00:27:03,266
and forgetting what kind of punk you are.

374
00:27:04,158 --> 00:27:06,333
Leave while you're still alive.

375
00:27:07,878 --> 00:27:09,278
Aren't you going to ask this time?

376
00:27:09,302 --> 00:27:11,566
What brings me to Korea?

377
00:27:12,650 --> 00:27:14,914
Just stick to your word.

378
00:27:14,938 --> 00:27:16,799
This is your final warning.

379
00:27:21,358 --> 00:27:24,138
I'll stick to my word.

380
00:27:24,162 --> 00:27:27,699
Because you'll come looking for me first anyway.

381
00:27:28,882 --> 00:27:30,942
And when that happens,

382
00:27:30,966 --> 00:27:34,999
what choice will you make then, Yoo Bo Na?

383
00:27:40,666 --> 00:27:42,706
[Caller ID Restricted: You keep your promises well]

384
00:27:44,182 --> 00:27:46,390
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong] Goodnight, Tae Seong.

385
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:49,133
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

386
00:28:05,366 --> 00:28:08,399
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

387
00:28:15,894 --> 00:28:19,766
Why'd you ask me to come to such a secluded place?

388
00:28:26,166 --> 00:28:28,099
Are you Kingfisher?

389
00:28:30,099 --> 00:28:32,258
Are you seriously asking me that?

390
00:28:32,282 --> 00:28:34,075
The World Cup case and the Haegong-dong case.

391
00:28:34,099 --> 00:28:36,610
You were there for both major incidents.

392
00:28:36,634 --> 00:28:38,730
The odds of that are practically impossible.

393
00:28:38,754 --> 00:28:40,326
Are you still drunk?

394
00:28:40,350 --> 00:28:42,462
I'm a reporter, you punk!

395
00:28:42,486 --> 00:28:46,599
Tell me. Everything that happened that day. I'm not joking.

396
00:28:51,194 --> 00:28:55,399
The seven-year-old boy who was at the scene in Haegong-dong.

397
00:28:56,042 --> 00:28:58,262
What? Why are you bringing that up?

398
00:28:58,286 --> 00:28:59,475
If I didn't know about it,

399
00:28:59,499 --> 00:29:01,798
that means it was never opened up to the press to protect that kid.

400
00:29:01,822 --> 00:29:03,390
Right, so?

401
00:29:03,414 --> 00:29:06,466
So I have an embargo too.

402
00:29:09,838 --> 00:29:11,538
What?

403
00:29:13,658 --> 00:29:16,299
I have someone I need to protect too.

404
00:29:21,299 --> 00:29:22,942
Let me ask you one thing.

405
00:29:22,966 --> 00:29:27,799
Are you sure the man you saw that day was Kingfisher?

406
00:29:31,166 --> 00:29:32,430
What about you?

407
00:29:32,454 --> 00:29:36,233
Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son was there and still pulled the trigger?

408
00:29:42,094 --> 00:29:46,142
I already heard it, and I can't pretend I haven't.

409
00:29:46,166 --> 00:29:49,286
If that man really was Kingfisher, then you're a witness.

410
00:29:49,310 --> 00:29:52,566
If not, you could be throwing the investigation off course. Got it?

411
00:29:53,633 --> 00:29:54,610
I know.

412
00:29:54,634 --> 00:29:56,475
I can't wait long.

413
00:29:56,499 --> 00:29:58,133
Whatever the reason, figure it out and tell me soon.

414
00:29:58,157 --> 00:30:00,466
Otherwise, I'll force the truth out of you.

415
00:30:01,698 --> 00:30:03,314
You know that, right?

416
00:30:03,338 --> 00:30:05,038
Oh, jeez.

417
00:30:15,166 --> 00:30:19,333
Your wife and your child,

418
00:30:20,038 --> 00:30:22,042
your family could be in danger.

419
00:30:22,066 --> 00:30:28,974
[Four Years Ago, The Night of "That Day"]

420
00:30:31,182 --> 00:30:32,966
Honey, what's wrong?

421
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:36,730
You're barely eating. Is something wrong?

422
00:30:36,754 --> 00:30:38,922
No.

423
00:30:38,946 --> 00:30:40,646
Nothing's wrong.

424
00:30:42,138 --> 00:30:43,838
This is so good.

425
00:30:45,622 --> 00:30:48,738
By the way, didn't you say you had something to show me?

426
00:30:48,762 --> 00:30:51,266
- Yeah.
- What is it?

427
00:30:55,450 --> 00:30:56,942
What is it?

428
00:30:56,966 --> 00:30:58,699
Look at this.

429
00:30:59,870 --> 00:31:01,599
What is it?

430
00:31:10,754 --> 00:31:14,166
I went to the hospital today, and I...

431
00:31:20,134 --> 00:31:21,834
What a relief

432
00:31:22,586 --> 00:31:24,466
to be able to come back.

433
00:31:25,726 --> 00:31:27,426
Tae Seong.

434
00:31:29,602 --> 00:31:31,598
Are you crying?

435
00:31:31,622 --> 00:31:33,714
I'm not.

436
00:31:33,738 --> 00:31:35,990
To come back to you, Bo Na,

437
00:31:36,014 --> 00:31:39,294
and to our baby.

438
00:31:39,318 --> 00:31:41,166
I'm just so relieved.

439
00:31:41,934 --> 00:31:43,822
Are you crying again?

440
00:31:43,846 --> 00:31:44,823
Are you a crybaby?

441
00:31:44,847 --> 00:31:48,098
No, I'm not. I'm just happy. I'm happy.

442
00:31:48,122 --> 00:31:51,699
I'm not crying. Why are you crying?

443
00:32:01,814 --> 00:32:04,033
They said this is the gestational sac.

444
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:08,306
Oh, my.

445
00:32:22,826 --> 00:32:25,942
Wow! It's orange.

446
00:32:25,966 --> 00:32:27,850
What color will it be?

447
00:32:27,874 --> 00:32:30,206
What's inside the orange?

448
00:32:30,230 --> 00:32:34,126
Ta-da! Wow, it's green.

449
00:32:34,150 --> 00:32:35,127
This is in here too...

450
00:32:35,151 --> 00:32:37,475
Just as I thought, those two are your Achilles' heels.

451
00:32:37,499 --> 00:32:43,366
Having something to protect is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

452
00:32:44,942 --> 00:32:47,199
It came out blue!

453
00:32:50,170 --> 00:32:51,706
- Mommy, why?
- Huh?

454
00:32:51,730 --> 00:32:52,926
Mommy, what's wrong?

455
00:32:52,950 --> 00:32:56,754
Mommy? I'm recharging my happiness.

456
00:32:56,778 --> 00:33:01,009
Holding Yul like this fills Mommy's happiness battery.

457
00:33:01,033 --> 00:33:02,886
Me too! Happiness recharge!

458
00:33:02,910 --> 00:33:04,610
You too?

459
00:33:19,399 --> 00:33:22,366
[Durumi Electronics]

460
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:25,614
Returned. It was useful.

461
00:33:25,638 --> 00:33:27,466
Just this? What about the others?

462
00:33:27,490 --> 00:33:29,650
I sent those somewhere.

463
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:32,266
Don't charge it as an expense. Just bill me for it.

464
00:33:42,630 --> 00:33:44,154
Gwangjang Market?

465
00:33:44,178 --> 00:33:45,909
I guess he was craving some mung bean pancakes.

466
00:33:45,933 --> 00:33:47,602
So, that ugly mug is here?

467
00:33:47,626 --> 00:33:48,806
Tracking down restaurants?

468
00:33:48,830 --> 00:33:51,114
It doesn't look like he came all this way just for a food tour.

469
00:33:51,138 --> 00:33:53,166
Please share this with me.

470
00:34:00,578 --> 00:34:03,255
Oh, that looks good.

471
00:34:03,279 --> 00:34:04,979
[Incoming Call]

472
00:34:07,090 --> 00:34:08,118
Not here.

473
00:34:08,142 --> 00:34:09,710
Looks like they got away.

474
00:34:09,734 --> 00:34:13,033
And Yoo Bo Na doesn't seem to know yet.

475
00:34:15,858 --> 00:34:17,550
Me?

476
00:34:17,574 --> 00:34:19,342
Well, since I'm here,

477
00:34:19,366 --> 00:34:22,475
maybe I'll check out some good restaurants nearby.

478
00:34:22,499 --> 00:34:24,499
There are tons of great places to eat in Korea.

479
00:34:27,950 --> 00:34:29,650
Mr. Kwon!

480
00:34:31,014 --> 00:34:32,794
Mr. Kwon!

481
00:34:32,818 --> 00:34:34,030
Yeah?

482
00:34:34,054 --> 00:34:38,299
What were you thinking about so deeply that you didn't even hear me calling?

483
00:34:39,314 --> 00:34:42,438
Well, if you heard a voice again that you first heard four years ago,

484
00:34:42,462 --> 00:34:44,538
do you think you'd recognize it?

485
00:34:44,562 --> 00:34:46,262
Huh?

486
00:34:47,622 --> 00:34:49,030
I'm not sure.

487
00:34:49,054 --> 00:34:54,462
Maybe if it's a familiar voice I hear all the time, like a singer or actor,

488
00:34:55,298 --> 00:34:57,554
but just hearing it once? That's tough.

489
00:34:57,578 --> 00:34:59,999
Why do you ask?

490
00:35:00,666 --> 00:35:02,366
Never mind.

491
00:35:03,666 --> 00:35:05,850
Let's get to the meeting.

492
00:35:05,874 --> 00:35:10,270
Did you find out how many of the parolees were violent offenders?

493
00:35:10,294 --> 00:35:13,194
I pulled the data from the past ten years and analyzed it.

494
00:35:13,218 --> 00:35:15,982
[Number of Parolees by Violent Crime Type] It's broken down by violent crime type,

495
00:35:16,006 --> 00:35:18,686
including murder, drugs, and sexual assault.

496
00:35:18,710 --> 00:35:22,966
And this is a separate list of violent offenders released this year.

497
00:35:23,899 --> 00:35:26,599
You must've spent days on this.

498
00:35:27,833 --> 00:35:29,699
[2026 Violent Offenders Released on Parole]

499
00:35:30,633 --> 00:35:32,899
[Jang Eun Hak, Assault Resulting in Death]

500
00:35:35,386 --> 00:35:38,366
Mr. Kwon, what's wrong? Are you okay?

501
00:35:41,566 --> 00:35:44,266
[Model Prisoner]

502
00:35:58,374 --> 00:35:59,758
What about you?

503
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:03,466
Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son was there and still pulled the trigger?

504
00:36:08,010 --> 00:36:09,710
Mr. Lee!

505
00:36:10,386 --> 00:36:12,478
I got the victim statements from the couple assault case.

506
00:36:12,502 --> 00:36:14,566
What should I do? Should I ask the cybercrime unit for assistance?

507
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:16,770
Yeah, go ahead. And let me know if you find anything.

508
00:36:16,794 --> 00:36:18,494
Alright.

509
00:36:21,418 --> 00:36:23,799
What are you looking at so intently...

510
00:36:24,838 --> 00:36:26,226
The Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

511
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:27,950
Why this case?

512
00:36:29,214 --> 00:36:30,218
Why aren't you asking me about it?

513
00:36:30,242 --> 00:36:32,158
About what?

514
00:36:32,182 --> 00:36:35,414
Oh, you mean the part about him being killed in front of his son?

515
00:36:35,438 --> 00:36:37,086
That's just speculation, you know.

516
00:36:37,110 --> 00:36:40,020
Honestly, I don't think Kingfisher would have pulled the trigger

517
00:36:40,044 --> 00:36:42,166
knowing there was a kid there.

518
00:36:42,190 --> 00:36:43,766
Well, look here.

519
00:36:43,790 --> 00:36:45,606
The windows in a Gosiwon are pretty small, right?

520
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:49,733
Couldn't there have been a blind spot from the sniper's position?

521
00:36:54,582 --> 00:36:56,414
Beom.

522
00:36:56,438 --> 00:36:58,790
Leave work early today.

523
00:36:58,814 --> 00:37:00,514
Leave work?

524
00:37:01,118 --> 00:37:02,454
Are you telling me to go home?

525
00:37:02,478 --> 00:37:04,338
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong] You mean, not working late?

526
00:37:04,362 --> 00:37:06,942
Then do you want to work late?

527
00:37:06,966 --> 00:37:09,033
You're sure it's okay?

528
00:37:10,354 --> 00:37:11,331
Yay!

529
00:37:11,355 --> 00:37:12,642
No taking it back, okay?

530
00:37:12,666 --> 00:37:16,099
Then I'll stop by the cybercrime unit and head straight home.

531
00:37:17,842 --> 00:37:19,542
Sir, yes, sir!

532
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:23,166
- Hey, where are you going?
- I'm going home! I'm off!

533
00:37:23,966 --> 00:37:25,866
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

534
00:37:26,874 --> 00:37:29,066
Is the embargo over already?

535
00:37:30,286 --> 00:37:32,675
If you're calling me, just say what's up. What is it?

536
00:37:32,699 --> 00:37:33,676
Dong Jin.

537
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:37,330
Why are you calling me so sweetly? You're making me nervous.

538
00:37:37,354 --> 00:37:39,333
What's up? What's happening?

539
00:37:40,454 --> 00:37:41,754
That punk's been released.

540
00:37:41,778 --> 00:37:44,882
That punk? Which punk?

541
00:37:44,906 --> 00:37:47,133
He was released on parole a month ago.

542
00:37:50,198 --> 00:37:51,898
What?

543
00:37:54,333 --> 00:37:58,754
The so-called Gangmyeon-dong Supermarket Murder Case.

544
00:37:58,778 --> 00:38:00,650
[Client Information] The perpetrator, Jang Eun Hak,

545
00:38:00,674 --> 00:38:02,494
brutally murdered a married couple

546
00:38:02,518 --> 00:38:05,394
who ran a neighborhood supermarket with a broken soju bottle,

547
00:38:05,418 --> 00:38:07,866
fled the scene, and was caught four years later.

548
00:38:07,890 --> 00:38:12,136
He was sentenced to 16 years in prison, but he was paroled last month,

549
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,575
just one year before his sentence was due to end.

550
00:38:14,599 --> 00:38:15,822
[Dongwoon Furniture] Hello.

551
00:38:15,846 --> 00:38:17,899
Oh, hello.

552
00:38:19,199 --> 00:38:20,515
- Are you looking for a bed?
- Yeah.

553
00:38:20,539 --> 00:38:23,133
What size bed are you looking for?

554
00:38:28,830 --> 00:38:30,794
Mr. Jang!

555
00:38:30,818 --> 00:38:32,062
Mr. Jang!

556
00:38:32,086 --> 00:38:35,046
- Oh, yeah.
- Move that.

557
00:38:35,070 --> 00:38:37,333
Oh, yes, understood.

558
00:38:38,982 --> 00:38:41,466
Oh, dear.

559
00:38:42,494 --> 00:38:46,546
Two people were brutally murdered, and he only got 16 years?

560
00:38:46,570 --> 00:38:47,566
What?

561
00:38:47,590 --> 00:38:50,758
He was convicted of death resulting from assault, not murder?

562
00:38:50,782 --> 00:38:51,786
That's right.

563
00:38:51,810 --> 00:38:53,390
He was 100 won short for soju,

564
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:55,982
got into a scuffle, and ended up committing murder.

565
00:38:56,006 --> 00:39:00,222
Then in court, he begged and pleaded, claiming he was drunk and felt humiliated,

566
00:39:00,246 --> 00:39:03,438
so he did what he did.

567
00:39:03,462 --> 00:39:05,354
He exploited the leniency of the law.

568
00:39:05,378 --> 00:39:06,610
They say the law has mercy.

569
00:39:06,634 --> 00:39:10,746
Jeez, the victims' families shed tears of blood.

570
00:39:10,770 --> 00:39:13,110
They do.

571
00:39:13,134 --> 00:39:15,099
Tears that never dry.

572
00:39:17,958 --> 00:39:22,799
But there's one notable detail there.

573
00:39:23,638 --> 00:39:27,850
The victim's family has a son,

574
00:39:27,874 --> 00:39:31,433
[Lee Dong Jin, 17 at the time] and he's a detective.

575
00:39:32,486 --> 00:39:35,750
What's even more interesting is that

576
00:39:35,774 --> 00:39:38,333
he was once assigned to a Kingfisher case.

577
00:39:39,678 --> 00:39:42,115
Wow, what an irony.

578
00:39:42,139 --> 00:39:46,014
A police officer whose family was victimized by a crime, chasing Kingfisher.

579
00:39:46,038 --> 00:39:48,638
With such a light sentence, he must be devastated to find out

580
00:39:48,662 --> 00:39:50,094
the guy even got parole.

581
00:39:50,118 --> 00:39:52,533
Not devastated. Furious.

582
00:39:53,531 --> 00:39:55,762
Do you think he might do something dangerous?

583
00:39:55,786 --> 00:39:56,802
I know.

584
00:39:56,826 --> 00:40:00,133
He's a cop, and he has a gun.

585
00:40:00,814 --> 00:40:03,133
No. He's not that kind of person.

586
00:40:03,810 --> 00:40:07,438
If he wanted personal revenge, he wouldn't have become a cop.

587
00:40:07,462 --> 00:40:10,626
He believes in making criminals pay within the law.

588
00:40:10,650 --> 00:40:12,466
That's what the police are there for.

589
00:40:24,033 --> 00:40:27,133
[Seoul Nambu Police Station, Lee Dong Jin]

590
00:40:31,934 --> 00:40:33,554
Se Ah.

591
00:40:33,578 --> 00:40:34,654
A date?

592
00:40:34,678 --> 00:40:36,633
Just the two of us?

593
00:40:37,590 --> 00:40:40,090
Really? Then where should we meet?

594
00:40:40,114 --> 00:40:42,066
Meeting one-on-one outside...

595
00:40:42,090 --> 00:40:44,834
Classic sister-in-law move, summoning her brother's wife like this.

596
00:40:44,858 --> 00:40:47,866
Still, isn't a sister-in-law easier to deal with than a mother-in-law?

597
00:40:47,890 --> 00:40:51,125
There's a reason they say a meddling sister-in-law is even worse.

598
00:40:51,149 --> 00:40:55,299
She's in trouble, or she's about to be.

599
00:41:07,818 --> 00:41:09,946
If you find anything, please let me know right away.

600
00:41:09,970 --> 00:41:11,670
Sir, yes, sir!

601
00:41:18,362 --> 00:41:21,442
I'm leaving work on time for the first time in a million years.

602
00:41:21,466 --> 00:41:22,978
Want to hit the arcade?

603
00:41:23,002 --> 00:41:24,826
Nope. I've got a date.

604
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:26,550
A date?

605
00:41:27,964 --> 00:41:29,021
With a guy?

606
00:41:29,045 --> 00:41:30,745
With my sister-in-law.

607
00:41:31,370 --> 00:41:33,399
Figures.

608
00:41:36,190 --> 00:41:38,758
Then what should I do?

609
00:41:38,782 --> 00:41:39,870
Bo Na, over here.

610
00:41:39,894 --> 00:41:42,202
They say this place is seriously good.

611
00:41:42,226 --> 00:41:44,246
- Wow!
- Looks like there's no line today.

612
00:41:44,270 --> 00:41:46,089
- Welcome.
- Table for two.

613
00:41:46,113 --> 00:41:47,735
- Do you have a reservation?
- No.

614
00:41:47,759 --> 00:41:50,578
You have to book through our app before you come.

615
00:41:50,602 --> 00:41:52,734
- Through an app?
- Yeah, I'm sorry.

616
00:41:52,758 --> 00:41:55,070
Then would you like to wait?

617
00:41:55,094 --> 00:41:56,794
[Waitlist] Wait...

618
00:41:57,418 --> 00:41:58,422
There are like 20 people waiting.

619
00:41:58,446 --> 00:41:59,942
- What do we do?
- Number 35!

620
00:41:59,966 --> 00:42:02,066
- Yes.
- This way, please.

621
00:42:03,370 --> 00:42:04,578
Thank you.

622
00:42:04,602 --> 00:42:05,609
Enjoy your food.

623
00:42:05,633 --> 00:42:06,809
Start with this, like this.

624
00:42:06,833 --> 00:42:08,409
Oh, Bo Na, wait.

625
00:42:08,433 --> 00:42:10,433
No? Right now

626
00:42:16,250 --> 00:42:18,999
Bo Na, should we take a picture together?

627
00:42:21,133 --> 00:42:22,309
Don't look at the camera.

628
00:42:22,333 --> 00:42:23,942
Yes, pretend you're not looking and act casual.

629
00:42:23,966 --> 00:42:25,330
Try to look as pretty as possible.

630
00:42:25,354 --> 00:42:27,866
Two? Give me a pretty pose!

631
00:42:27,890 --> 00:42:29,175
- That's so cute.
- Ta-da!

632
00:42:29,199 --> 00:42:30,364
How is it?

633
00:42:30,388 --> 00:42:31,675
Oh, my, you look like a bunny!

634
00:42:31,699 --> 00:42:33,899
- How do you do this? A heart.
- A heart.

635
00:42:38,726 --> 00:42:41,902
Mom, you're really something else, huh?

636
00:42:41,926 --> 00:42:45,954
You badmouth Bo Na, but you still make her all those side dishes.

637
00:42:45,978 --> 00:42:48,770
Oh, please. What are you talking about?

638
00:42:48,794 --> 00:42:50,594
Am I doing it for her?

639
00:42:50,618 --> 00:42:53,594
I make it to feed my own son.

640
00:42:53,618 --> 00:42:57,309
Oh, dear. Other mothers-in-law pack all kinds of food

641
00:42:57,333 --> 00:42:59,090
for their sons-in-law.

642
00:42:59,114 --> 00:43:01,074
Jeez, there you go again.

643
00:43:01,098 --> 00:43:03,278
- I'm exhausted.
- Oh, you're here?

644
00:43:03,302 --> 00:43:04,982
Sun II, please get me a glass of water.

645
00:43:05,006 --> 00:43:06,594
Alright.

646
00:43:06,618 --> 00:43:07,770
Where did you go?

647
00:43:07,794 --> 00:43:09,758
Oh, the department store.

648
00:43:09,782 --> 00:43:13,226
You know we're meeting Jun Woo's future in-laws the day after tomorrow.

649
00:43:13,250 --> 00:43:16,175
Oh, right. Your second son's wedding date is set.

650
00:43:16,199 --> 00:43:17,176
But why the department store?

651
00:43:17,200 --> 00:43:19,946
Well, I need something decent to wear.

652
00:43:19,970 --> 00:43:23,258
Seon Ja, what did you wear for Tae Seong's family meeting?

653
00:43:23,282 --> 00:43:24,810
What?

654
00:43:24,834 --> 00:43:27,050
Well, just something simple.

655
00:43:27,074 --> 00:43:29,694
Oh, right. You never had one, did you?

656
00:43:29,718 --> 00:43:32,690
Oh, lucky you. You had it easy.

657
00:43:32,714 --> 00:43:34,138
Oh, my back.

658
00:43:34,162 --> 00:43:35,734
What do you mean I didn't have one?

659
00:43:35,758 --> 00:43:38,886
I did it twice for Sun II and Du Ri.

660
00:43:38,910 --> 00:43:43,066
Is meeting your daughter's in-laws the same as meeting your son's?

661
00:43:44,374 --> 00:43:47,433
They're basically the same.

662
00:43:48,633 --> 00:43:52,554
You can tell what kind of family you're dealing with by meeting the parents.

663
00:43:52,578 --> 00:43:55,970
Both of our future in-laws are educators.

664
00:43:55,994 --> 00:43:59,850
Maybe that's why their daughter is so well-mannered,

665
00:43:59,874 --> 00:44:02,502
and her face is so bright, without a shadow.

666
00:44:02,526 --> 00:44:06,233
You can just tell she grew up surrounded by love.

667
00:44:07,134 --> 00:44:11,046
Oh, dear. Is it a little awkward saying this in front of you?

668
00:44:11,070 --> 00:44:12,375
- Your daughter-in-law...
- You punk!

669
00:44:12,399 --> 00:44:13,742
- Shut your mouth!
- Oh, my.

670
00:44:13,766 --> 00:44:14,909
Oh, my, what's gotten into you?

671
00:44:14,933 --> 00:44:16,606
Oh, my. What did I even do?

672
00:44:16,630 --> 00:44:20,346
Fine. I never had a formal family meeting, and I don't have any in-laws.

673
00:44:20,370 --> 00:44:22,109
Because my daughter-in-law is an orphan.

674
00:44:22,133 --> 00:44:24,038
So what? What about it?

675
00:44:24,062 --> 00:44:25,870
Did you contribute anything?

676
00:44:25,894 --> 00:44:28,650
Well, I gave quite a lot for the wedding gift.

677
00:44:28,674 --> 00:44:31,914
Why are you making such a fuss over getting an orphaned daughter-in-law?

678
00:44:31,938 --> 00:44:34,502
Wow, I've been friends with you all my life...

679
00:44:34,526 --> 00:44:36,390
You little punk. I'm going to get you today.

680
00:44:36,414 --> 00:44:37,642
Oh, my. Oh, my!

681
00:44:37,666 --> 00:44:39,566
- Mom!
- What's gotten into you?

682
00:44:42,510 --> 00:44:44,210
Wow!

683
00:44:47,666 --> 00:44:51,194
Se Ah, what do you usually do when you hang out with your friends?

684
00:44:51,218 --> 00:44:52,434
Me?

685
00:44:52,458 --> 00:44:56,933
We'd go for chicken feet and soju. Or cold pork belly and beer.

686
00:44:58,918 --> 00:45:00,666
Was it that obvious?

687
00:45:02,233 --> 00:45:05,723
Actually, I did some research before I came.

688
00:45:05,747 --> 00:45:08,875
I was wondering what young people do for fun these days.

689
00:45:08,899 --> 00:45:11,409
Like the place we went to earlier.

690
00:45:11,433 --> 00:45:16,433
It's not really my thing, but I thought you might enjoy it.

691
00:45:17,362 --> 00:45:19,833
So it was your first time.

692
00:45:22,599 --> 00:45:27,833
I actually love just sitting around doing nothing with you.

693
00:45:28,899 --> 00:45:29,950
Really?

694
00:45:29,974 --> 00:45:31,733
Yeah.

695
00:45:34,374 --> 00:45:37,602
Then where do you actually go most often?

696
00:45:37,626 --> 00:45:39,281
Let's have that be our last stop.

697
00:45:39,305 --> 00:45:41,005
Is that what you want?

698
00:45:42,250 --> 00:45:45,066
There's one place.

699
00:45:48,066 --> 00:45:50,133
[Se Dol, You Have a New Message]

700
00:45:54,482 --> 00:45:57,099
Get to the PC bang now.

701
00:46:03,474 --> 00:46:05,042
Hey, why are you so late?

702
00:46:05,066 --> 00:46:06,475
You said you were leaving work on time.

703
00:46:06,499 --> 00:46:08,206
Huh?

704
00:46:08,230 --> 00:46:12,638
I went somewhere else first. What, you think you're my only friend?

705
00:46:12,662 --> 00:46:14,709
Hey, say hi. This is my sister-in-law.

706
00:46:14,733 --> 00:46:16,598
Bo Na, this is my friend, Mr. Tiger.

707
00:46:16,622 --> 00:46:18,575
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

708
00:46:18,599 --> 00:46:20,275
I didn't know your friend was a guy.

709
00:46:20,299 --> 00:46:21,442
Is he your boyfriend?

710
00:46:21,466 --> 00:46:23,615
No, we're just friends.

711
00:46:23,639 --> 00:46:25,706
Nice to meet you properly.

712
00:46:25,730 --> 00:46:27,206
I'm Beom Seong Hun.

713
00:46:27,230 --> 00:46:29,409
I'm really sorry I couldn't make it to the wedding.

714
00:46:29,433 --> 00:46:32,198
Oh, don't be.

715
00:46:32,222 --> 00:46:34,599
- He's handsome.
- What?

716
00:46:35,654 --> 00:46:38,075
Then, let's skip the formalities and sit down.

717
00:46:38,099 --> 00:46:40,714
Alright, your only mission today is

718
00:46:40,738 --> 00:46:45,091
to show my sister-in-law the true taste of victory. Got it?

719
00:46:45,115 --> 00:46:47,509
Well, that's a lot of weight on my shoulders.

720
00:46:47,533 --> 00:46:49,433
I'm counting on you.

721
00:46:50,438 --> 00:46:53,818
Bo Na, since my friend's here, want to try an FPS game?

722
00:46:53,842 --> 00:46:55,054
FPS?

723
00:46:55,078 --> 00:46:59,530
When you're stressed, nothing beats shooting things.

724
00:46:59,554 --> 00:47:01,178
Bang, bang!

725
00:47:01,202 --> 00:47:03,110
Sniping.

726
00:47:03,134 --> 00:47:05,302
There's a game where you snipe people?

727
00:47:05,326 --> 00:47:08,709
Yeah, it's a little difficult.

728
00:47:08,733 --> 00:47:11,109
But you can just stick with us, and you'll be fine.

729
00:47:11,133 --> 00:47:14,830
He'll do all the killing anyway.

730
00:47:14,854 --> 00:47:15,942
Please take care of me.

731
00:47:15,966 --> 00:47:16,943
Oh, come on.

732
00:47:16,967 --> 00:47:19,475
I'm not that good.

733
00:47:19,499 --> 00:47:21,542
Okay, shall we give it a try?

734
00:47:21,566 --> 00:47:23,266
Sure.

735
00:47:26,034 --> 00:47:28,818
There, there's someone over there. SW 1 direction.

736
00:47:28,842 --> 00:47:30,150
Oh, okay, got it.

737
00:47:30,174 --> 00:47:32,090
Oh, nice.

738
00:47:32,114 --> 00:47:33,398
Well, it's nothing.

739
00:47:33,422 --> 00:47:34,662
Watch out, there's one more.

740
00:47:34,686 --> 00:47:37,390
Hey, behind that wall. See him?

741
00:47:37,414 --> 00:47:39,094
Wow, what's gotten into you?

742
00:47:39,118 --> 00:47:40,109
Hey, ping one, ping one.

743
00:47:40,133 --> 00:47:42,375
Oh, yeah! Assist!

744
00:47:42,399 --> 00:47:44,375
Oh, your aim is really good today.

745
00:47:44,399 --> 00:47:46,299
What's with the sudden praise?

746
00:47:48,022 --> 00:47:50,775
Oh, why are you so good today?

747
00:47:50,799 --> 00:47:51,902
I'll take care of him.

748
00:47:51,926 --> 00:47:54,342
- One team left, one team.
- Okay.

749
00:47:54,366 --> 00:47:57,742
I smell chicken.

750
00:47:57,766 --> 00:47:58,842
What is it?

751
00:47:58,866 --> 00:48:00,442
This feels like a chicken dinner.

752
00:48:00,466 --> 00:48:03,209
[Match in progress in the marked zone. 45 seconds left]

753
00:48:03,233 --> 00:48:04,966
Chicken!

754
00:48:06,299 --> 00:48:07,842
Bo Na, how was it? Winning's fun, right?

755
00:48:07,866 --> 00:48:10,433
It's so much fun.

756
00:48:11,399 --> 00:48:12,438
This is really fun.

757
00:48:12,462 --> 00:48:13,714
- Right?
- Yeah.

758
00:48:13,738 --> 00:48:18,834
Hey, thanks to you, my years of pent-up stress are gone!

759
00:48:18,858 --> 00:48:20,438
You were great.

760
00:48:20,462 --> 00:48:21,706
No, it wasn't me.

761
00:48:21,730 --> 00:48:23,430
What do you mean?

762
00:48:25,342 --> 00:48:26,630
[We Won! Chicken for Dinner Tonight!] What?

763
00:48:26,654 --> 00:48:28,286
Three kills?

764
00:48:28,310 --> 00:48:29,766
You only got three kills?

765
00:48:29,790 --> 00:48:31,694
Then, how did we even win?

766
00:48:31,718 --> 00:48:33,526
Come with me.

767
00:48:33,550 --> 00:48:35,606
[Team Rank 1, 15 Kills] Huh?

768
00:48:35,630 --> 00:48:38,102
Bo Na, what is this?

769
00:48:38,126 --> 00:48:39,294
What?

770
00:48:39,318 --> 00:48:41,846
You got all those kills!

771
00:48:41,870 --> 00:48:43,106
This isn't your first time, is it?

772
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:45,554
I think we just discovered your hidden talent.

773
00:48:45,578 --> 00:48:49,209
Were you a sniper in a past life?

774
00:48:49,233 --> 00:48:50,210
Maybe I was.

775
00:48:50,234 --> 00:48:53,510
- This is amazing!
- I guess I got lucky today.

776
00:48:53,534 --> 00:48:55,758
Well, let's play one more round.

777
00:48:55,782 --> 00:48:57,075
- You want to?
- Yeah.

778
00:48:57,099 --> 00:48:58,442
Alright.

779
00:48:58,466 --> 00:49:00,409
This game isn't exactly easy.

780
00:49:00,433 --> 00:49:03,133
[13 Kills, 14 Kills, 16 Kills]

781
00:49:04,477 --> 00:49:06,177
[17 Kills]

782
00:49:14,625 --> 00:49:16,325
Oh, dear.

783
00:49:20,299 --> 00:49:22,526
[Team Rank 1, 19 Kills]

784
00:49:22,550 --> 00:49:23,754
Wow...

785
00:49:23,778 --> 00:49:25,442
No way...

786
00:49:25,466 --> 00:49:28,033
This isn't possible.

787
00:49:29,458 --> 00:49:34,109
Se Ah must've been enjoying herself to keep you out that late.

788
00:49:34,133 --> 00:49:36,409
I had so much fun.

789
00:49:36,433 --> 00:49:39,310
I got to try a lot of things I'd never done before. It was really fun.

790
00:49:39,334 --> 00:49:42,110
Looks like Se Ah really did something big today.

791
00:49:42,134 --> 00:49:45,075
It's okay. Take your time.

792
00:49:45,099 --> 00:49:47,642
I'm going to take Yul to the store later.

793
00:49:47,666 --> 00:49:48,978
Sun II said to bring over some fresh kimchi.

794
00:49:49,002 --> 00:49:51,130
Really? I love your mom's fresh kimchi.

795
00:49:51,154 --> 00:49:52,510
Please bring lots.

796
00:49:52,534 --> 00:49:57,410
Today I discovered a side of my sister-in-law that completely blew me away.

797
00:49:57,434 --> 00:49:58,878
Isn't she seriously cool?

798
00:49:58,902 --> 00:50:01,582
How old is your brother's kid again?

799
00:50:01,606 --> 00:50:04,406
Yul? Four? Why do you ask that?

800
00:50:04,430 --> 00:50:07,266
Then the timing lines up perfectly, huh?

801
00:50:08,278 --> 00:50:09,609
You know I have a good gut feeling, right?

802
00:50:09,633 --> 00:50:11,930
What, you?

803
00:50:11,954 --> 00:50:14,099
I think your sister-in-law

804
00:50:16,430 --> 00:50:18,730
might be hiding her true identity.

805
00:50:18,754 --> 00:50:20,722
What identity?

806
00:50:20,746 --> 00:50:24,266
The legend who vanished without a trace in the spring four years ago

807
00:50:26,594 --> 00:50:28,218
the legend of FPS games!

808
00:50:28,242 --> 00:50:30,609
But she was on maternity leave.

809
00:50:30,633 --> 00:50:34,510
A gaming genius who shows up every few years and sweeps the top records?

810
00:50:34,534 --> 00:50:36,109
Enough with the nonsense!

811
00:50:36,133 --> 00:50:38,194
Okay.

812
00:50:38,218 --> 00:50:39,918
Well

813
00:50:42,282 --> 00:50:46,742
Bo Na, were you surprised when I suddenly asked you out today?

814
00:50:46,766 --> 00:50:50,638
No. I was just... excited.

815
00:50:50,662 --> 00:50:54,498
It's been so long since I've gone out and had fun without Yul. It was exciting.

816
00:50:54,522 --> 00:50:56,030
Really?

817
00:50:56,054 --> 00:51:00,262
So you haven't really seen your friends since you had Yul?

818
00:51:00,286 --> 00:51:03,182
I guess I don't really have many friends.

819
00:51:03,206 --> 00:51:04,575
I'm not sure why.

820
00:51:04,599 --> 00:51:07,146
Oh, I see.

821
00:51:07,170 --> 00:51:11,654
I feel like I got a little closer to you today.

822
00:51:11,678 --> 00:51:13,546
You do?

823
00:51:13,570 --> 00:51:17,990
Actually, there was something I wanted to ask you.

824
00:51:18,014 --> 00:51:21,318
That's partly why I asked you out.

825
00:51:21,342 --> 00:51:23,630
But I've changed my mind.

826
00:51:23,654 --> 00:51:25,774
I'm going to ask you for something else!

827
00:51:25,798 --> 00:51:26,986
What is it?

828
00:51:27,010 --> 00:51:31,798
From now on, please speak casually with me.

829
00:51:31,822 --> 00:51:36,566
I'm Tae Seong's younger sister, and we're family.

830
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:39,994
Okay, should we do that then?

831
00:51:40,018 --> 00:51:41,538
Really? Oh, yeah!

832
00:51:41,562 --> 00:51:43,030
What a rewarding day!

833
00:51:43,054 --> 00:51:46,042
Then can I link arms with you?

834
00:51:46,066 --> 00:51:47,206
Sure, come here.

835
00:51:47,230 --> 00:51:49,233
Oh, really?

836
00:51:51,846 --> 00:51:53,675
This is nice!

837
00:51:53,699 --> 00:51:55,475
[Tae Seong Chicken]

838
00:51:55,499 --> 00:51:58,802
Mom, are you still mad?

839
00:51:58,826 --> 00:52:00,338
You really hold a grudge.

840
00:52:00,362 --> 00:52:03,675
Come on, it's not like her saying rude things is anything new.

841
00:52:03,699 --> 00:52:06,630
Still, you don't like it when others badmouth your daughter-in-law, do you?

842
00:52:06,654 --> 00:52:09,160
Of course I don't, huh?

843
00:52:09,184 --> 00:52:10,678
She's my daughter now too.

844
00:52:10,702 --> 00:52:13,834
If anyone's going to criticize her, it should be me. Who is she?

845
00:52:13,858 --> 00:52:16,794
What, "bright"?

846
00:52:16,818 --> 00:52:18,618
Is that supposed to mean my girl is dark and dull?

847
00:52:18,642 --> 00:52:20,509
Oh, my. "My girl"?

848
00:52:20,533 --> 00:52:22,034
That darn punk.

849
00:52:22,058 --> 00:52:23,970
Who's bragging?

850
00:52:23,994 --> 00:52:26,089
I hated the orphan daughter-in-law too,

851
00:52:26,113 --> 00:52:28,666
and I was annoyed about not having a meeting with her family.

852
00:52:28,690 --> 00:52:31,666
- Mom!
- What mom in this world

853
00:52:31,690 --> 00:52:34,809
wants to give her precious son to an orphan?

854
00:52:34,833 --> 00:52:36,254
But as time went by...

855
00:52:36,278 --> 00:52:38,099
Mom!

856
00:52:50,114 --> 00:52:52,237
Oh, you're here?

857
00:52:52,261 --> 00:52:53,961
Yes, Mother.

858
00:52:55,402 --> 00:52:58,233
Wait, how are you two together again...

859
00:53:01,257 --> 00:53:03,109
Honey, take Yul outside first.

860
00:53:03,133 --> 00:53:04,110
Huh?

861
00:53:04,134 --> 00:53:06,566
Please. Just go. I'm asking you.

862
00:53:08,062 --> 00:53:09,442
[Red Bean Bread] Mother, have this when you get hungry.

863
00:53:09,466 --> 00:53:10,450
It's your favorite red bean bread.

864
00:53:10,474 --> 00:53:13,499
Oh, okay. Thank you.

865
00:53:23,233 --> 00:53:25,399
[Red Bean Bread]

866
00:53:27,466 --> 00:53:31,399
You should've told me you were bringing her with you.

867
00:53:32,630 --> 00:53:34,966
Did you eat dinner?

868
00:53:37,050 --> 00:53:39,238
Mom.

869
00:53:39,262 --> 00:53:41,209
Apologize to Yul's mom.

870
00:53:41,233 --> 00:53:46,018
Well, I didn't say it for her to hear.

871
00:53:46,042 --> 00:53:48,133
But she heard you.

872
00:53:49,750 --> 00:53:52,854
Did I make anything up?

873
00:53:52,878 --> 00:53:55,286
She is an orphan.

874
00:53:55,310 --> 00:53:57,130
Mom!

875
00:53:57,154 --> 00:54:00,250
Just because she's an orphan doesn't mean you can treat her however you want.

876
00:54:00,274 --> 00:54:02,966
What did I do...

877
00:54:05,848 --> 00:54:09,496
So what? What if I say I can't apologize?

878
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:12,299
What? Are you going to stop seeing me?

879
00:54:25,978 --> 00:54:30,105
Jeez, they say raising kids is useless.

880
00:54:30,129 --> 00:54:33,554
All you care about is how precious your wife is.

881
00:54:33,578 --> 00:54:35,278
Mom.

882
00:54:35,966 --> 00:54:37,418
Mom, honestly, you're sorry, aren't you?

883
00:54:37,442 --> 00:54:39,618
Sorry for what?

884
00:54:39,642 --> 00:54:43,033
People even talk bad about the president in private. What's the big deal?

885
00:54:44,430 --> 00:54:48,233
Why did they have to walk in at that exact moment and make such a fuss?

886
00:54:49,934 --> 00:54:52,999
What lousy timing.

887
00:54:59,202 --> 00:55:00,466
I'm sorry.

888
00:55:00,490 --> 00:55:02,766
I'll apologize on her behalf.

889
00:55:04,394 --> 00:55:07,450
Me? I'm fine.

890
00:55:07,474 --> 00:55:09,566
It doesn't bother me.

891
00:55:12,538 --> 00:55:14,775
She's your mom.

892
00:55:14,799 --> 00:55:16,209
Maybe it's because I'm a mom too?

893
00:55:16,233 --> 00:55:19,899
I think I understand a little.

894
00:55:20,911 --> 00:55:23,733
That feeling of being helpless in front of your child.

895
00:55:24,382 --> 00:55:27,999
That instinct to put your child first.

896
00:55:33,010 --> 00:55:37,133
Being a mom doesn't excuse everything. She was still wrong.

897
00:55:40,802 --> 00:55:44,114
Then should I tell you exactly what I think?

898
00:55:44,138 --> 00:55:46,499
Isn't your mom being a little too much?

899
00:55:47,833 --> 00:55:51,190
Well, I'm not the person I used to be.

900
00:55:51,214 --> 00:55:52,594
I'm not alone anymore.

901
00:55:52,618 --> 00:55:54,609
I have a husband and a daughter.

902
00:55:54,633 --> 00:55:58,046
I have a mother-in-law and three sisters-in-law.

903
00:55:58,070 --> 00:56:01,399
What matters is the present, not the past. Isn't it?

904
00:56:05,506 --> 00:56:07,206
But

905
00:56:08,366 --> 00:56:11,375
I believe she'll understand someday.

906
00:56:11,399 --> 00:56:14,033
If we keep arguing and making up like this...

907
00:56:15,533 --> 00:56:17,766
Look at you, saying things like that.

908
00:56:18,466 --> 00:56:22,198
I mean, we laugh and cry together,

909
00:56:22,222 --> 00:56:26,730
get on each other's nerves, hurt each other...

910
00:56:26,754 --> 00:56:28,899
Isn't that what family is?

911
00:56:29,678 --> 00:56:32,999
So we're really going at it.

912
00:56:34,374 --> 00:56:36,633
Going at it? What are we going at?

913
00:56:37,434 --> 00:56:39,393
What do you want to eat, Yul?

914
00:56:39,417 --> 00:56:41,338
Should we stir-fry Yul's favorite sausages?

915
00:56:41,362 --> 00:56:43,442
Yeah, I like sausages.

916
00:56:43,466 --> 00:56:44,809
Let's go stir-fry some sausages.

917
00:56:44,833 --> 00:56:47,533
Let's go make some sausages!

918
00:57:13,830 --> 00:57:16,142
Why are the lights off?

919
00:57:16,166 --> 00:57:18,033
Are they closed already?

920
00:57:21,433 --> 00:57:24,899
The door isn't even locked. What's going on?

921
00:57:49,878 --> 00:57:51,675
Mom.

922
00:57:51,699 --> 00:57:53,399
Mom.

923
00:57:54,099 --> 00:57:55,833
Dad.

924
00:58:16,733 --> 00:58:19,875
[Dongwoon Furniture]

925
00:58:19,899 --> 00:58:21,702
Twenty percent off for a set.

926
00:58:21,726 --> 00:58:24,414
Welcome. Can I help you find anything?

927
00:58:24,438 --> 00:58:25,942
I'm just looking around.

928
00:58:25,966 --> 00:58:27,933
Sure. Take your time.

929
00:58:28,733 --> 00:58:31,329
Just write your address here.

930
00:58:31,353 --> 00:58:34,609
We'll have it delivered by truck tomorrow.

931
00:58:34,633 --> 00:58:37,633
[Dongwoon Furniture, We Sell the Cheapest]

932
00:58:38,730 --> 00:58:40,433
I'm back.

933
00:58:45,234 --> 00:58:48,758
You left for that delivery ages ago. Why are you only getting back now?

934
00:58:48,782 --> 00:58:50,674
Were you goofing off somewhere again?

935
00:58:50,698 --> 00:58:55,568
No. I took a wrong turn on the way. I'm sorry.

936
00:58:55,592 --> 00:58:58,226
And what about the chair delivered to Taeheung-dong this morning?

937
00:58:58,250 --> 00:59:02,760
What did you do this time? We got a complaint saying one leg is wobbly.

938
00:59:02,784 --> 00:59:04,010
What?

939
00:59:04,034 --> 00:59:06,409
Well... that can't be right.

940
00:59:06,433 --> 00:59:10,418
How many times have I told you to be careful when carrying things up and down?

941
00:59:10,442 --> 00:59:14,006
Why do you keep making us go back for repairs? Oh, my.

942
00:59:14,030 --> 00:59:16,942
How am I supposed to keep you on like this?

943
00:59:16,966 --> 00:59:19,042
I'm sorry. I'll make sure it doesn't happen again.

944
00:59:19,066 --> 00:59:21,694
Forget it! Go back to work.

945
00:59:21,718 --> 00:59:23,266
Jeez.

946
00:59:23,290 --> 00:59:25,066
I'm sorry.

947
00:59:25,715 --> 00:59:29,333
Jeez, that punk is really on my case. Darn it.

948
00:59:36,299 --> 00:59:38,666
[Dongwoon Furniture]

949
00:59:51,402 --> 00:59:53,333
Darn it.

950
01:01:06,305 --> 01:01:08,805
Darn it! Seriously!

951
01:01:27,650 --> 01:01:29,350
Hey!

952
01:01:31,677 --> 01:01:33,377
You punk!

953
01:01:34,594 --> 01:01:36,299
Honey!

954
01:01:38,402 --> 01:01:42,130
So why did you keep ignoring me? Why?

955
01:01:42,154 --> 01:01:44,342
Why?

956
01:01:44,366 --> 01:01:46,066
You punk!

957
01:01:48,846 --> 01:01:51,933
Police! Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

958
01:01:57,690 --> 01:01:58,942
Shoot me.

959
01:01:58,966 --> 01:02:01,640
Go ahead. Shoot me, you punk!

960
01:02:01,664 --> 01:02:04,642
If you want to see her die right here...

961
01:02:04,666 --> 01:02:08,866
Please help me...

962
01:02:12,666 --> 01:02:14,826
Last warning.

963
01:02:14,850 --> 01:02:16,174
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

964
01:02:16,198 --> 01:02:19,856
Who on earth are you to tell me what to do, you punk?

965
01:02:19,880 --> 01:02:21,858
I'll decide what to do with my own knife, you punk!

966
01:02:21,882 --> 01:02:22,866
Jang Eun Hak!

967
01:02:22,890 --> 01:02:26,402
Please help me.

968
01:02:26,426 --> 01:02:27,642
Help me.

969
01:02:27,666 --> 01:02:31,326
Please help me.

970
01:02:31,350 --> 01:02:33,314
Let the woman go.

971
01:02:33,338 --> 01:02:38,519
I'm going to kill every punk who looks down on me!

972
01:02:38,543 --> 01:02:40,242
You little punks, huh?

973
01:02:40,266 --> 01:02:41,909
Hey, you looked down on me too, didn't you?

974
01:02:41,933 --> 01:02:43,633
You little...

975
01:02:50,433 --> 01:02:51,410
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

976
01:02:51,434 --> 01:02:53,566
Honey, honey!

977
01:03:00,266 --> 01:03:01,999
Jang Eun Hak!

978
01:03:04,798 --> 01:03:07,042
Apply pressure to stop the bleeding and call an ambulance.

979
01:03:07,066 --> 01:03:08,766
Hurry!

980
01:03:20,322 --> 01:03:22,022
Hey!

981
01:03:36,278 --> 01:03:38,399
You punk, stop right there!

982
01:03:43,318 --> 01:03:45,033
Jang Eun Hak!

983
01:03:50,946 --> 01:03:52,646
Hey!

984
01:03:55,350 --> 01:03:57,050
Stop!

985
01:03:58,674 --> 01:04:01,066
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

986
01:04:01,866 --> 01:04:03,799
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

987
01:04:17,306 --> 01:04:19,006
Dong Jin!

988
01:05:19,738 --> 01:05:21,678
Dong Jin!

989
01:05:21,702 --> 01:05:24,775
What if you run into your husband?

990
01:05:24,799 --> 01:05:27,422
Tae Seong, what do I do?

991
01:05:27,446 --> 01:05:29,570
You should get out of there for now.

992
01:05:29,594 --> 01:05:32,975
The area was huge, so I'm not sure we covered every route.

993
01:05:32,999 --> 01:05:35,575
So we don't know where something could come from.

994
01:05:35,599 --> 01:05:37,209
Guess what I found?

995
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:39,478
Mommy.

996
01:05:39,502 --> 01:05:42,858
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect. And you know that, right?

997
01:05:42,882 --> 01:05:44,638
I'll do my job,

998
01:05:44,662 --> 01:05:45,794
[Resignation Letter] so you do yours.

999
01:05:45,818 --> 01:05:47,286
You're a reporter.

1000
01:05:47,310 --> 01:05:49,142
[An Exclusive, Kingfisher...] My husband has his work to do,

1001
01:05:49,166 --> 01:05:51,733
and I have mine...
